{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1379 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b9148d0e30ef70fab53b1fefd8e3bec95868cfd09d9149bb543c23b1e2092c68" :edb/db-before-t 1378 :edb/db-after-t 1379 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534691 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:18:24.677Z" 13194139534691 true] [17592186096586 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303641 13194139534691 true] [17592186096586 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303645 13194139534691 true] [17592186096586 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303669 13194139534691 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303614 13194139534691 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303635 13194139534691 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303638 13194139534691 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303661 13194139534691 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303665 13194139534691 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303621 13194139534691 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303628 13194139534691 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303651 13194139534691 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303654 13194139534691 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303657 13194139534691 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303648 13194139534691 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303676 13194139534691 true] [17592186096850 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534691 true] [17592186096850 1100 "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186096850 1100 "What is $∫\\sin 3x\\cos 3xdx$?" 13194139534691 false] [17592186096850 1145 "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186292523 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186292523 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534691 false] [17592186303614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303615 13194139534691 true] [17592186303614 1089 "q-114696" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534691 true] [17592186303614 1100 "Calculate $\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303614 1113 #uuid "5e06f254-9ae0-5c9b-85c7-9e6e4070e958" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303614 1145 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\theta =x$ and substituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {(2{cos}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the same formula $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1$ with $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\frac{3}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+\\frac{3}{2}\\,x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303616 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303617 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303618 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303619 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303620 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1041 "selection" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303619 13194139534691 true] [17592186303615 1110 #uuid "d65407ce-aa3d-565c-8639-4943b98cc9f4" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303616 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303616 1111 #uuid "303fa97f-3d61-5184-a349-c12f8c8074bf" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303617 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303617 1111 #uuid "5fe4ba27-02f7-5c91-9f48-1a56dab35618" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303618 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303618 1111 #uuid "b4b3d3e2-ebdd-5027-9f80-9ab86295e47c" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303619 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303619 1111 #uuid "9fae57e2-8599-5683-863f-a150d85259c6" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303620 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303620 1111 #uuid "2ec8596c-f498-545c-ad50-8a9b0f32a482" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303622 13194139534691 true] [17592186303621 1089 "q-114706" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534691 true] [17592186303621 1100 "$\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303621 1113 #uuid "4323046d-0eea-5be0-a5b7-ac027795bcc6" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303621 1145 "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (2\\cdot 2{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x-2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303623 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303624 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303625 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303626 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303627 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1041 "selection" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303624 13194139534691 true] [17592186303622 1110 #uuid "af6e7734-0646-5022-9cd7-6630c6f083fe" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303623 1034 "-{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303623 1111 #uuid "82a62c8c-484c-5495-b1b7-5f5850631915" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303624 1034 "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303624 1111 #uuid "e351c5e5-ab8b-59db-9b5e-19896b7eccad" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303625 1034 "3{x}^{2}-2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303625 1111 #uuid "c5db3896-3524-5c26-a73f-323d24950fa4" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303626 1034 "{x}^{2}-x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303626 1111 #uuid "c113ef7a-beb6-5603-95df-92ad4f197e39" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303627 1034 "-{x}^{2}+x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303627 1111 #uuid "904d90a7-bfff-5e62-81a0-59241dac5e67" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303629 13194139534691 true] [17592186303628 1089 "q-114709" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534691 true] [17592186303628 1100 "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303628 1113 #uuid "c4dc5f61-51e0-57b7-9717-0e7b5d819bec" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303628 1145 "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303630 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303631 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303632 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303633 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303634 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1041 "selection" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303634 13194139534691 true] [17592186303629 1110 #uuid "184b4d0f-01c1-54e3-9c60-6a883c5b3e9f" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303630 1034 "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303630 1111 #uuid "d43de327-f14f-5993-b86b-37f87c7eb6bb" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303631 1034 "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303631 1111 #uuid "9c1ea649-8300-5c98-ab16-994898b76d4d" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303632 1034 "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303632 1111 #uuid "8eeeb9d9-00a8-5f46-9313-37622780ab11" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303633 1034 "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303633 1111 #uuid "49cc67b2-e806-56cd-a818-e2d53cbf4609" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303634 1034 "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303634 1111 #uuid "c679b82c-12a6-5579-aa35-c0922a857353" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303635 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303636 13194139534691 true] [17592186303635 1089 "q-347179" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303635 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534691 true] [17592186303635 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b163cd4cc1add41ae2c043b4b3d7d818dd9b23de0a4b762bc85d348c0bca4def.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\pi $ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303635 1113 #uuid "ffc0ed13-441c-5653-8f7c-66f8bb3ae58b" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303635 1145 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2x)\\,|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot (-\\pi ))+2(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =(0+\\pi )-(0-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\pi  \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303637 13194139534691 true] [17592186303636 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534691 true] [17592186303636 1041 "field-1" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303636 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303637 13194139534691 true] [17592186303636 1110 #uuid "694ddeb6-b4bf-5f6e-8bbc-2bb046085ac3" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303637 1034 "3\\pi" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303637 1111 #uuid "5c9c73e6-97df-51de-91dc-19edd1d6fc14" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303639 13194139534691 true] [17592186303638 1089 "q-347182" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534691 true] [17592186303638 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303638 1113 #uuid "7e6a604d-c591-56e2-a8f3-63cd2a5f1e21" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303638 1145 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303640 13194139534691 true] [17592186303639 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534691 true] [17592186303639 1041 "field-1" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303639 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303640 13194139534691 true] [17592186303639 1110 #uuid "d17d2d99-482a-5e96-a7f8-10615a206c45" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303640 1034 "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303640 1111 #uuid "d5dd8e22-4e53-5097-9663-141d62fb9e32" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303641 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303642 13194139534691 true] [17592186303641 1089 "q-348715" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303641 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534691 true] [17592186303641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303641 1113 #uuid "3b1100b1-bd62-51d2-8f07-e50972013e35" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303641 1145 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303643 13194139534691 true] [17592186303642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303644 13194139534691 true] [17592186303642 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534691 true] [17592186303642 1041 "field-1" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303642 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303643 13194139534691 true] [17592186303642 1110 #uuid "fcdb6414-d340-5241-913f-a7e0fdf66c27" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303643 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303643 1111 #uuid "3e35dce5-cd92-5b28-a495-352005bf7737" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303644 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534691 true] [17592186303644 1111 #uuid "7f143a12-9050-5856-8db5-5ee5c6c21f43" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303645 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303646 13194139534691 true] [17592186303645 1089 "q-348716" 13194139534691 true] [17592186303645 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534691 true] [17592186303645 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/a2ccde221d71e611f7917d6dac0d12ca6b8204d9cd80a21d79005195245cf77a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{